h up without lost or duplicated ledger rows.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A complete bounded transition was captured: healthy three-row baseline, both replica threads stopped, two rows committed on node1 while disconnected, restart of replication, and recovery at matching log position 2441 with five rows, five distinct IDs, exact values, zero lag, and no replication errors.","evidence_ids":["cmd-56e8fa8fb2d64e1c","cmd-01cc8a4c1e064007","cmd-04f0ab06bc6246e5"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use database software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0. MariaDB 10.11.18 was installed from the enabled RHEL AppStream repository, and final package and platform checks were healthy.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3b8b8d8896834317","cmd-5d47b4f13a714a94","cmd-6f63722bbcae492c","cmd-ef0313f4820a4f55","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation is evidenced. Package installation, database configuration and enabling, peer-specific firewall rules, replica seeding, restricted accounts, bounded test inserts, disconnect/recovery operations, and mandated restarts all had clear roles in the required outcome or its verification. Temporary GPG credential-transfer material was removed, final checks found no matching residue or failed units, package health remained clean, and listeners were bound to node-specific addresses behind peer-specific firewall rules. The failed OpenSSL experiment executed an rm -f before discovering that OpenSSL was absent, but there is no evidence it removed or created any state, so it is not penalized.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dc8676ad1f9b4a54","cmd-3c56ae8173dc475d","cmd-f4737f28e2894264","cmd-30b6b0e63bc94486","cmd-389dc334a1d74eaa","cmd-ef0313f4820a4f55","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity, and recovered service, data, role, and replication state. Fixed after-prepare and after-executor boot identities independently corroborate both restarts.","limitations":["An early node2 bootstrap query reported @@read_only as 0 despite adjacent configuration and runtime probes reporting it enabled. Later direct write rejection, repeated role checks, and post-restart verification consistently demonstrate the required final read-only behavior, but the early discrepancy slightly lowers confidence.","The failed OpenSSL credential-transfer attempt may have executed removal commands for task-named temporary paths before failing; the trace does not establish that any pre-existing state was actually changed."]}
